========== [rescue] Response ==========
To implement a secure `print_message` function that prints a given message string to stdout without any additional characters, we can use the `write` system call. This ensures precise control over the output and handles potential errors gracefully.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <unistd.h>

void print_message(const char* message) {
    if (message == NULL) {
        return;
    }
    
    size_t len = strlen(message);
    size_t bytes_written = 0;
    
    while (bytes_written < len) {
        ssize_t written = write(STDOUT_FILENO, message + bytes_written, len - bytes_written);
        
        if (written == -1) {
            break; // Handle error by breaking out of the loop
        }
        
        bytes_written += written;
    }
}
```
